The drift direction is perpendicular to the beam direction as indicated by the arrows in the figure. By implementing a perpendicular drift to the beam axis, the analog storage capabilities of the TPC's are optimized, allowing for a minimum in the number of required channels of electronics. However, because of the perpendicular-drifting electrons, this requires the TPC's to be situated so that no magnetic field is present from the solenoid. This is accomplished by positioning XTPC's 7 meters from the interaction region.

